<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Donetsk-Krivoy Rog Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Kharkiv</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bolshevik republic of the Donbas and Kryvyi Rih industrial regions, proclaimed in 1918 as part of Soviet Russia rather than Ukraine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In February 1918 a regional congress of soviets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkiv</a> proclaimed the Donetsk-Krivoy Rog Soviet Republic over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and iron districts of eastern and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Its leader, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fyodor-sergeyev">Fyodor Sergeyev</a>, known as Artyom, argued that the industrial region belonged economically with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> rather than with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a council of people's commissars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkiv</a> and tried to nationalise mines and factories, but it existed for only a few weeks. Its separate status was opposed by Bolsheviks who backed a single <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets">Soviet Ukraine</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> did not formally recognise it as distinct from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, German and Austro-Hungarian forces advanced into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donbas">Donbas</a>. The government retreated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luhansk">Luhansk</a> and beyond, and by spring 1918 the republic was dissolved into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets">Soviet Ukraine</a>'s structures, with its territory occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/donetsk-krivoy-rog-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Donetsk-Krivoy Rog Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kharkiv</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Fyodor Sergeyev (Artyom)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Donetsk-Kryvyi Rih Soviet Republic, DKR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=donetsk-krivoy-rog-soviet-republic" aria-label="Donetsk-Krivoy Rog Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5510 438 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Donetsk-Krivoy Rog Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5830 694L5820 533M5830 694L5830 694"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M5830 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5830 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5830 694h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kharkiv. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=donetsk-krivoy-rog-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
